      <div class="logic-title">The useful habit: ask which assumption breaks</div>
      <div class="logic-copy">The Sorites paradox pressures vague predicates like "heap" and "bald." The Ship of Theseus pressures identity through time. The Fermi paradox pressures estimates about life, technology, and detectability in a galaxy with roughly 100 to 400 billion stars. Olbers' paradox looked at a dark night sky and refuted an infinite, eternal, static universe before modern cosmology supplied the mechanism: the observable universe has finite age and is expanding.</div>
